Relay: small read buffer while idle, batched writes while busy, lazy BufferedConn reader

N.Relay copies with sing's bufio.Copy. For a source that is neither a socket
nor a read waiter (TLS, REALITY and other TLS-based outbounds: the download
side of a proxied connection) that copy takes a 32 KiB pool buffer before
every read, so an idle connection holds one for as long as it stays open, and
during a transfer every decrypted TLS record goes to the inbound socket with a
write(2) of its own. Every inbound connection is also wrapped in a
BufferedConn whose 4 KiB bufio.Reader was made at once and kept for the whole
relay once the connection had been peeked.

- copyConn (relay_copy.go) is bufio.Copy with another fallback for such
  sources: it reads into a 2 KiB buffer while the connection looks idle and
  into full pool buffers while data keeps coming (a read that fills the small
  buffer switches up, two short reads in a row switch back). Cached data,
  Vision's replaceable reader/writer, splice and read waiters (sockets,
  Shadowsocks) keep bufio.Copy's code paths.
- While a transfer runs on full buffers and the destination unwraps to a
  socket, a reader goroutine reads up to 8 buffers ahead and the copy writes
  everything read meanwhile with one writev(2) (relay_batch.go). It never waits
  for data: when the burst ends the source goes back to the copy loop, so an
  idle connection has no extra goroutine and holds no extra buffer.
- BufferedConn makes its reader on first use, reads without one go straight
  to the conn, and ReaderReplaceable drops a drained reader when the relay
  unwraps the conn.

Ported from getmikan/Citrus (GPL-3.0, author Nemu-x) common/net/relay_copy.go,
relay_batch.go and bufconn.go, commits 6c1d881e, d23b8008, 415e7791 (small
buffer), 316b3af7 (batching), 8c11680f and b00599ab (lazy reader), in the form
Rerowros/veles (GPL-3.0, commit f3d6ddaf, its P12) carries them. Not taken:
the parts that need Citrus' TLS fork (waiting on a TLS conn without a buffer)
or its AnyTLS queue, the 64 KiB socket reads and the scheduler yields of the
copy loops. Tests from Citrus (bufconn_test.go, relay_copy_test.go,
relay_batch_test.go), cut to what is ported.

